  "problem": "${\\int }_{-7}^{-5}(2{f}^{\u2032}(x)-4)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "We split the integral into the sum of two integrals and factor out the constants. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-7}^{-5}(2{f}^{\u2032}(x)-4)\\,\\text{d}x & =2{\\int }_{-7}^{-5}{f}^{\u2032}(x)\\,\\text{d}x-4{\\int }_{-7}^{-5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2f(x)\\,{|}_{-7}^{-5}-4x\\,{|}_{-7}^{-5} \\\\  & =2(f(-5)-f(-7))-4(-5-(-7)) \\\\  & =2((1+2\\sqrt{2})-1)-8 \\\\  & =2(1+2\\sqrt{2}-1)-8 \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{2}-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
